# BKYC PR descriptions

When the user asks for a PR description / PR body for any **BKYC** ticket (epic HDP-7636 or children, TaskAlloc BKYC, auth/gateway/actor permission packs), include these sections **minimally**. Apply to **all associated PRs** in a multi-repo pack (not only one).

ASCII hyphen-minus only (` - `, not em/en dashes).

## Required sections (order)

1. **Ticket / epic / what lands** - short; matrix or table OK.
2. **PR pack** - table of sibling PRs when multi-repo.
3. **Verify / Test plan** - technical as needed (SQL, checkboxes).
4. **How this fits the whole BKYC solution** - **visual mermaid flowchart only** (see below).
5. **Decisions / tradeoffs for reviewers** - short Decision / Why / Tradeoff table.
6. **Knowledge handoff (for whoever is waiting on this)** - exact codes + who consumes them + out of scope.

Optional: common-scripts commit links, rename callouts, sign-off comment links.

## How this fits - flowchart rules

- Use ` ```mermaid ` `flowchart TB` (or LR).
- **Plain English only** - roles and what people can **do** (business functionality).
- **Do not** put API names, Java method names, Flyway versions, permission codes, or usecase codes in the diagram.
- Permission / API codes belong in Knowledge handoff + Verify, not in the chart.
- Label the current PR with a plain sentence (e.g. "This PR seeds who is allowed to do what"), not repo jargon alone.
- Default role boxes (adapt per ticket):

| Audience | Capability language (examples) |
|---|---|
| Bank employee | View upload history; upload lead files; download bank response files |
| Corporate ops (CBC / CBF) | View tasks and progress; assign tasks to agents |
| Field agent (BCA / BFA) | Open assigned task; update status; submit completed BKYC |
| Report viewer (SPOC) | View BKYC reports / Superset (note if wired later) |

- Edges should describe outcomes in English (e.g. "Pick an eligible agent and assign or reassign a task"), not `getEligibleAgentsForTask`.

## Decisions / tradeoffs

Minimal table:

| Decision | Why | Tradeoff |
|---|---|---|

Only real choices reviewers might push back on (naming, scope cuts, deferred work, soft seeds). No essay.

## Knowledge handoff

- **Must use (do not rename)** - exact permission / story / usecase codes.
- DDP TaskAlloc: prefer `TASK-ALLOC-BKYC-*` - not legacy Excel `BKYC-UPLD-*` unless the ticket is explicitly Excel/DSA.
- Agent entitlement: current SoT is `TASK-BKYC` (Actor `TASK_BKYC`); story/usecase may stay `PRDCT-BKYC` / `PRDCT-BKYC-UC001` - call out if ticket still uses older `PRDCT-SERVICEREQUEST-BKYC`.
- After deploy / who waits: UAM, FE, eligible-agents, APK, Superset gateway, etc.
- **Out of scope** - one short line.

